HTSAdapter::associateToken(token) — branching-tree (BTT)
See the Testing section of the Solidity standards (branching-tree technique). Each leaf maps to a
named test in HTSAdapterTest.t.sol; a "given" is a state-setup modifier, a "when" is a parameter
branch, an "it should" is the asserted outcome. Source: HTSAdapterLib.associateToken().

associateToken(token)
├── given the caller does not hold HTS_MANAGER_ROLE
│   └── it should revert AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount   → test_AssociateToken_RevertsForOperatorWithoutManagerRole
└── given the caller holds HTS_MANAGER_ROLE
    ├── given the address is not an HTS token (HTS 167)
    │   └── it should revert HTSNotAToken                   → test_AssociateToken_RevertsWhenNotAToken
    ├── given the diamond is already associated (HTS 194)
    │   └── it should revert HTSTokenAlreadyAssociated      → test_AssociateToken_RevertsWhenAlreadyAssociated
    └── given the diamond is not associated yet
        └── it should associate and emit HTSTokenAssociated → test_AssociateToken_AssociatesTheDiamond
